But remember the premise of the OISD.

22:41.400 --> 22:44.540
In the passive observational data, the states look identical.

22:44.860 --> 22:45.080
Right.

22:45.240 --> 22:49.120
You don't have the labels because the divergence only manifests under an intervention.

22:49.120 --> 22:55.960
If you are training purely on passive data streams, the contrastive loss function has no gradient to follow.

22:55.960 --> 22:57.440
It's an inescapable trap.

22:57.760 --> 22:59.700
If you don't intervene, you don't see the difference.

22:59.800 --> 23:01.800
If you don't see the difference, you compress the states.

23:02.260 --> 23:06.140
If you compress the states, your safety guardrails are permanently blinded.

23:06.220 --> 23:08.800
Which is a terrifying realization for the industry.

23:09.020 --> 23:09.720
It really is.

23:09.800 --> 23:14.660
And, you know, this transitions us into what I consider the most audacious section of Flyxion's work.

